---
title: Skeleton & lazy load
description: What shows before the content does. A skeleton holds the shape of what is coming; a lazy picture fades up from a blur. Both keep the layout still, so nothing jumps on arrival.
eyebrow: Component
source: src/components/loading.css · src/js/im-media.js
---
<h2>Skeleton</h2>
<p>Size each piece with utilities. A skeleton should have the <em>shape</em> of what it stands for — that is the whole point.</p>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-auto" style="--im-grid-min: 15rem">
	<div aria-hidden="true"><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-media"></span><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-text w-1/4 mt-3"></span><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-title w-5/6"></span><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-text"></span><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-text w-2/3"></span></div>
	<div aria-hidden="true"><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-media"></span><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-text w-1/4 mt-3"></span><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-title w-3/4"></span><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-text"></span><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-text w-1/2"></span></div>
	<div aria-hidden="true"><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-media"></span><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-text w-1/4 mt-3"></span><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-title w-2/3"></span><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-text"></span><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-text w-4/5"></span></div>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h3>Pieces</h3>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-fit" style="--im-grid-min: 15rem; --im-grid-gap: 2rem">
	<div class="flex gap-3" aria-hidden="true"><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-circle size-10 shrink-0"></span><div class="grow"><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-text w-1/2"></span><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-text w-1/3"></span></div></div>
	<div aria-hidden="true"><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-title w-2/3"></span><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-text"></span><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-text"></span><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-text w-3/5"></span><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-btn mt-3"></span></div>
	<div class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: .75rem" aria-hidden="true"><div class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="im-skeleton size-12 shrink-0"></span><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-text grow"></span></div><div class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="im-skeleton size-12 shrink-0"></span><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-text grow"></span></div><div class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="im-skeleton size-12 shrink-0"></span><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-text grow"></span></div></div>
</div>
{{/example}}
<div class="im-table-scroll">
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Class</th><th></th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td><code>im-skeleton</code></td><td>A grey block with a light that sweeps across it. Size it yourself.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>-text</code> · <code>-title</code></td><td>A line of text; a heading. Heights are in <code>em</code>, so they match the type they stand for.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>-circle</code> · <code>-media</code> · <code>-btn</code></td><td>An avatar; a 16:10 picture; a button.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>-pulse</code></td><td>Breathes instead of sweeping — calmer when there are many on screen.</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h3>Swapping it for the real thing</h3>
<p>Wrap the region in <code>im-loading</code> with <code>aria-busy="true"</code>. When your script replaces the skeletons and sets <code>aria-busy="false"</code>, the content fades up. Press the button.</p>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: 1rem; max-width: 24rem">
	<div class="im-loading" id="load-demo" aria-busy="true" aria-live="polite"><div class="flex gap-3"><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-circle size-12 shrink-0"></span><div class="grow"><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-text w-1/2"></span><span class="im-skeleton im-skeleton-text"></span></div></div></div>
	<button class="im-btn im-btn-sm im-btn-outline self-start" type="button" onclick="const r=document.getElementById('load-demo'); const was=r.dataset.skel||(r.dataset.skel=r.innerHTML); const busy=r.getAttribute('aria-busy')==='true'; r.innerHTML=busy?'<div class=&quot;flex items-center gap-3&quot;><span class=&quot;im-avatar im-avatar-lg&quot; data-initial=&quot;S&quot;></span><div><strong class=&quot;block&quot;>Swarnil Singhai</strong><span class=&quot;text-sm text-muted&quot;>Engineer · Budapest</span></div></div>':was; r.setAttribute('aria-busy',String(!busy)); this.textContent=busy?'Reset':'Finish loading'">Finish loading</button>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Lazy pictures</h2>
<p><code>im-lazy</code> holds the picture's shape and shows a ground colour; the image — loaded by the browser's own <code>loading="lazy"</code> — sharpens in from a blur when it arrives. Scroll to these, or reload the page.</p>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-auto" style="--im-grid-min: 14rem">
	<span class="im-lazy" style="--im-lazy-ground: #4f8a8b"><img src="{{demo.three.[0].feature_image}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></span>
	<span class="im-lazy" style="--im-lazy-ground: #b08d6e"><img src="{{demo.three.[1].feature_image}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></span>
	<span class="im-lazy" style="--im-lazy-ground: #1d2733"><img src="{{demo.three.[2].feature_image}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></span>
</div>
{{/example}}
{{{{code "hbs"}}}}
<span class="im-lazy" style="--im-lazy-ratio: 16 / 10; --im-lazy-ground: #4f8a8b">
	<img src="{{img_url feature_image size="m"}}" alt="{{title}}" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
</span>
{{{{/code}}}}
<div class="im-table-scroll">
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th></th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td><code>--im-lazy-ratio</code></td><td>The shape to hold. 16 / 10.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>--im-lazy-ground</code></td><td>A colour close to the picture's average. Falls back to the surface grey.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>--im-lazy-src</code></td><td>Or a tiny blurred placeholder: <code>url(…)</code> of a 20-pixel-wide version.</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>Without <code>im-media.js</code> the picture is simply shown — the blur-up only engages once the head script has confirmed JavaScript, the same rule as <a href="/motion/animation/#reveal-on-scroll">scroll reveals</a>.</p>

<h2>Other loading states</h2>
<ul>
	<li>A button that is working: <code>aria-busy="true"</code> — see <a href="/components/button/#states">Button</a>.</li>
	<li>A spinner: <code>im-ring im-ring-spin</code> — see <a href="/components/progress/#ring">Progress</a>. Dots: <code>im-dots</code> — see <a href="/motion/animation/#loops">Animation</a>.</li>
	<li>More of a list: <a href="/navigation/pagination/#load-more">load more and infinite scroll</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Under about 300ms, show nothing.</strong> A skeleton that flashes for a moment is worse than a blank that is replaced at once.</p>
